      "id": "7a7665a62ed2996df5ab",
      "title": "Software Engineer (Modeling) R&D",
      "location": null,
      "url": "https://www.stream.security/positions/position-54_e6a",
      "description": "We're hiring Software Engineer (Modeling) - Stream.Security Product Customers Resources Company Sign in Back Autonomous Prevention Closes exploitable paths on its own, before anyone has to defend them Stream Force Define the mission. Agents build, run, and scale it. Autonomous Detection Follows the attack across every boundary, with no analyst driving it Autonomous Threat Hunting Hunts live production continuously, with no one starting the hunt Autonomous Remidation & Response Contains precisely. Closes the exposure. Integrations Check out our evergrowing list of integrations Autonomous cloud Defense goes Kubernetes New Goat scenarios turn 2025-2026's real Kubernetes and container-runtime research — rootkits, eBPF backdoors, runc escapes, and more — into automated attack chains you can run against your SOC. Back All Resources Learn about cloud detection and response Upcoming Events Meet our team at upcoming expos and events Blog Insights, product updates, and security tips Datasheets Technical overviews and product specifications Reports Research, analysis, and industry findings Webinars Join our live event or watch on demand Watch on demand Hands On: Building AI Agents You Can Actually Trust July 14, 2026 11:30 AM EST Back About Us Get to know our story and team Press News, articles and press resources Jobs Join us, we’re hiring! Contact Us Company Overview Download PDF Get a Demo Positions R&D Software Engineer (Modeling) Ramat Gan Full-time Stream Security’s platform constantly models enterprises’ cloud environments, empowering security teams to detect, investigate, and respond to threats in real time. Leveraging an event-driven architecture, the platform pinpoints how threats emerge and demystifies the impact of remediating them instantly. Our vision is a world where each day is safer and more secure than the one before. We are a company built on the foundation of challenging and disrupting the way things are done, and we’re looking for innovators who are as committed to shaping the future of cybersecurity as we are. We're backed by top global top-tier VCs well positioned to execute our vision. We seek excellent individuals to join our journey and build a legacy. This is a rare opportunity to join a startup on the ground floor. You will join a small but powerful R&D team that is ambitious and dynamic. We take pride in creating a hugely impactful product that is being built at the highest level of craft and execution and is already delighting multiple customers. What You'll Do: You will play a critical role in building and enhancing Stream Security’s cloud topology analysis platform, shaping the future of our product and company. · Build Cloud Posture Models : Code and maintain robust components that model entire cloud infrastructures, covering compute, security, networking, Kubernetes environments and IAM permissions. · Resource Topology Mapping : Establish a model of every component in public cloud environments to visualize connectivity and assess posture. · Drive Innovation : Use advanced methodologies and the latest technologies to deepen our understanding of cloud resource interconnections and posture. · End-to-End Feature Ownership : Collaborate with PMs to identify and prioritize needs, design scalable, production-ready solutions, and rapidly iterate based on user feedback. · Scale and Optimize : Push solutions to large-scale production, handling architectural constraints and ensuring robustness. Collaborate with cross-functional teams to move from prototype to scalable implementation. · Accountability for Delivery and Quality : Lead the development process with full ownership over timelines, quality, and production monitoring, ensuring continuous alignment with the company's objectives and resources. Requirements Mandatory: · 5+ years in software development , primarily in a SaaS environment using Agile methodologies as part of core or algorithm development teams working in one of the major public cloud providers (AWS, GCP or Azure). · BSc in Computer Science . · Knowledge of Graph Theory and graph algorithms. · Understanding of network topology and infrastructure with an emphasis of networking and security. · Python/Go experience. Advantages: · MSc in Computer Science · AWS Certified Solutions Architect , Azure Solutions Architect Expert and or similar credentials · Experience in cybersecurity . · Track record of deploying and optimizing large-scale cloud systems in production environment from a development perspective. Apply now If the form wasn’t loaded, please click here to apply . Product Autonomous Prevention Autonomous Detection Autonomous Threat Hunting Autonomous Remediation & Response Resources Book a demo Customers Blog Webinars CloudWiki Company About us Become a Partner Press Jobs Contact us © StreamSec Ltd. Copyright Policy Terms of Use Privacy",
